# Continuation stack exceeded (CEK limit)
#
# LLT's CEK evaluator has a continuation stack depth limit (MAX_CONTINUATION_STACK = 2048).
# This test verifies that exceeding the limit produces a clean error message.
#
# NOTE: This test is impractical to express as a corpus test because building a 2048-level
# expression requires either:
# 1. 2048+ nested brackets (exceeds lexer limit of 256)
# 2. Programmatic thunk construction (not available in .llt source)
#
# The functionality is tested in `eval_materialize.rs::test_max_continuation_stack_enforced`
# which constructs a 2100-deep chain of PendingBuiltin thunks programmatically.
#
# This file documents the expected error behavior:
# - Error code: E040 (DepthExceeded)
# - Message: "maximum evaluation depth exceeded (2048)"
# - Non-cacheable: thunk state is restored for retry
#
# If you need to test this interactively, use a deeply nested expression like:
# [$+ [$+ [$+ [$+ ... (2100 levels) ... 1] 1] 1] 1]
#
# But this will hit the lexer's bracket limit before reaching the continuation stack limit.

# Placeholder test — actual enforcement is in unit tests
